----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sylou's own images
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Each of Sylou's three images keeps Sylou's licence files and this NOTICE in
/licenses, and in /licenses/third-party the licence of every third-party part
it carries that does not keep its own elsewhere in the image:

  sylou-web        Built on nginx's nginx-unprivileged image (Alpine), whose
                   licence is in /usr/share/licenses/nginx. The packages the
                   app is built from: each one's own licence files, listed in
                   index.txt, and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md beside them.

  sylou-functions  Built on Supabase's edge-runtime image (Debian 12), whose
                   packages keep their licences in /usr/share/doc. The edge
                   runtime's own MIT licence; the packages the functions use,
                   each with its own licence files, listed in index.txt; and
                   the Apache 2.0 licence of PDF.js, which unpdf bundles.

  sylou-tools      Built on Deno's Alpine image. Deno's MIT licence, and those
                   of the Deno standard library and the Postgres driver the
                   tools load from deno.land.

The system packages of each base image keep the licence records their
publishers ship with them; each released image's SBOM lists them.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Supabase
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

supabase/postgres, supabase/gotrue and supabase/storage-api are published by
Supabase and carry their own licences. They are referenced by digest in
compose.yaml and are not redistributed here. supabase/edge-runtime is the base
of sylou-functions, above.

The database start-up scripts in sylou-local/db/ began as the corresponding
files in Supabase's self-hosting recipe (github.com/supabase/supabase, the
docker/volumes/db folder, tag self-hosted/v0.8.4), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0:

    Copyright (c) Supabase, Inc.

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License"); you may
    not use these files except in compliance with the License. You may obtain
    a copy of the License at

        http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

    Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
    distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS, WITHOUT
    WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the
    License for the specific language governing permissions and limitations
    under the License.

They have been changed for Sylou: each database role is given its own random
password, read from a file instead of an environment variable, and the signing
secret is no longer written into the database. The scripts Sylou does not use
(webhooks.sql, _supabase.sql, logs.sql, pooler.sql, realtime.sql) are not
included.

